{
 "name": "reversing-starter",
 "description": "Reversing (forward/reverse) DOL starter: KM1 feeds the motor in one phase order, KM2 swaps two phases for reverse. Electrical interlocking via NC aux contacts (KM2 21-22 in the forward path, KM1 21-22 in the reverse path) makes it impossible to energize both at once. Each direction seals in through its own aux contact; S0 stops; KK1 protects the motor. To physically reverse a running motor, press S0 first.",
